<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O) and FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection — Morphological realism / specimen match: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Segments the SHA-256-locked mammalian bronchial tree specimen (`datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/bronchial_tree_specimen.jpg`) via chromatic tissue separation, conducting airway vs alveolar sac cluster partitioning, Euclidean distance transform (EDT) lumen caliber mapping, and Zhang-Suen 1-pixel skeletonization (L522-652), extracting N = 32 3-arm bronchial junctions with mean branching angle 76.49 ± 14.61 deg (CV = 0.191, closely matching the 75.0 deg Planar/Orthogonal bifurcation and 68.0 deg Domain sprouting reference angles) and mean daughter-to-parent caliber ratio 0.8826 ± 0.1066." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
